WEBVTT

1
00:00:05.299 --> 00:00:13.020
[MUSIC]

2
00:00:14.226 --> 00:00:16.090
From a watchlist on the monitor tab,

3
00:00:16.090 --> 00:00:19.710
click the underlying symbol you wish
to create your options trade for.

4
00:00:21.110 --> 00:00:23.719
So long as your tabs are part
of the same windows group,

5
00:00:23.719 --> 00:00:26.290
the underlying will appear
in the order entry panel.

6
00:00:27.590 --> 00:00:29.418
To the right of the order entry panel,

7
00:00:29.418 --> 00:00:32.320
select option chain from
the drop down menu.

8
00:00:32.320 --> 00:00:35.424
The option chain display shows
call options to the left and

9
00:00:35.424 --> 00:00:38.350
put options to the right of
the central strike column.

10
00:00:39.700 --> 00:00:40.876
You will see the price and

11
00:00:40.876 --> 00:00:44.080
the daily change of the underlying
to the upper right of the window.

12
00:00:45.370 --> 00:00:49.322
Above the call area you'll see tabs for
different expirations.

13
00:00:49.322 --> 00:00:53.040
Click a tab or
to locate additional expiration dates.

14
00:00:53.040 --> 00:00:54.430
Click on the More Tab.

15
00:00:55.960 --> 00:00:59.480
Above the footer area, you'll see
a drop down menu for strike prices.

16
00:01:00.730 --> 00:01:02.374
Access this menu to change or

17
00:01:02.374 --> 00:01:05.740
refine the number of strike
prices displayed on the page.

18
00:01:07.140 --> 00:01:11.214
Hovering the cursor above any bid
price displays a red background.

19
00:01:11.214 --> 00:01:14.052
This indicates that by
clicking on the field,

20
00:01:14.052 --> 00:01:16.830
it would create an order
to sell that option.

21
00:01:18.160 --> 00:01:22.332
Hovering above any ask price displays
a blue background indicating that by

22
00:01:22.332 --> 00:01:26.050
clicking on this field,
it would create an order to buy an option.

23
00:01:27.340 --> 00:01:30.626
Clicking a single strike will
close the option chain window and

24
00:01:30.626 --> 00:01:33.790
populates the order entry panel
with the chosen option leg.

25
00:01:35.030 --> 00:01:38.216
Locate the desired option
strike you want to transact,

26
00:01:38.216 --> 00:01:42.770
click on the relevant price field,
which will close the option chain display.

27
00:01:44.280 --> 00:01:48.129
Use the order entry panel to define
the quantity of options to trade.

28
00:01:48.129 --> 00:01:51.030
Choose the right order type
from the drop down menu.

29
00:01:52.270 --> 00:01:56.277
If using a limit price, choose the value
by clicking in the input field, or

30
00:01:56.277 --> 00:01:57.820
simply typing in the value.

31
00:01:59.180 --> 00:02:03.570
Select from the time and force drop
down whether this is a day or GTC order.

32
00:02:04.890 --> 00:02:06.740
Your order is ready to review.

33
00:02:06.740 --> 00:02:09.570
Click the Submit button to
generate an order confirmation.

34
00:02:10.990 --> 00:02:13.380
When you have reviewed
the details click Transmit.

35
00:02:14.660 --> 00:02:17.193
The order is sent for
execution at the exchange and

36
00:02:17.193 --> 00:02:20.340
will appear in the activity panel
to the lower left of mosaic.

37
00:02:21.580 --> 00:02:26.049
To pause or interact with an active order,
click on it in the activity panel and

38
00:02:26.049 --> 00:02:27.619
make the relevant choice.

39
00:02:27.619 --> 00:02:28.119
[MUSIC]